10079 0 obj
  << /ActualText (This audit covers UFarm\054 a platform that turns real\055world assets \050RWAs\051 into tokens on EVM chains\056 It is built on the ERC\0553643 permissioned token standard\056 Each asset is issued as an ERC\05520 compatible security token\054 and only verified investors can hold or transfer it\056 Investors are verified off\055chain \050KYC\057KYB\057AML\051\054 and the rules are enforced on\055chain through identity registries and a compliance module\056\nThe review was conducted over a week period and included a comprehensive analysis of the relevant smart contracts\056 It covered the ERC\0553643 token suite and its identity and compliance modules\054 the factory that deploys a full token suite for each asset\054 the private credit token with its investment and withdrawal settlement flows\054 the private credit value aggregator\054 and the fixed\055price sale contract\056\nDuring the assessment\054 we did not identify any critical or high\055severity issues\056 We identified one medium\055severity finding\072 the withdrawal settlement flow does not take a holder\047s frozen token balance into account\056 As a result\054 settlements revert and holders with partially frozen balances cannot redeem or move their tokens until an agent removes the freeze\056 In addition\054 we identified one low\055severity finding and five informational issues\056\nAll identified issues were either remediated or acknowledged by the development team and subsequently verified by our auditors\056\nFollowing the remediation phase\054 we conclude that the protocol\047s overall security posture and code quality have improved as a result of this audit\056)
     /K [ 1 ]
     /P 10080 0 R
     /Pg 764 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

