10312 0 obj
  << /ActualText (The two limits are evaluated independently over overlapping parts of the same balance\054 so an outgoing transfer is capped at balanceOf \055 max\050reserved\054 frozen\051 instead of balanceOf \055 reserved \055 frozen\056 The holder can therefore move out min\050reserved\054 frozen\051 more than the invariant allows\072\nthe holder has a balance x \075 1000 with y \075 100 frozen\054 and reserves z \075 400\056 The request is accepted because 400 \053 100 \074\075 1000\056\nthe holder transfers x \055 z \075 600 out\056 It passes the reserved check \050600 \074\075 1000 \055 400\051 and the free balance check \050600 \074\075 1000 \055 100\051\056\nthe holder is left with a balance of 400\054 400 reserved and 100 frozen\054 so reserved \053 frozen \075 500 \076 balance \075 400\056\nsettleWithdrawals\050\051 then tries to burn the 400 reserved units while \137requireFreeBalance\050\051 only sees 400 \055 100 \075 300 available\054 and reverts\056\nThe reservation can never be settled\056 There is no entry point to cancel a withdrawal request\054 and because reservedWithdrawal \075\075 balanceOf\054 the holder can no longer transfer anything either\054 so the position becomes completely immobile\056\nNote that this is distinct from the case where an agent freezes tokens after a request has been made\056 Here no further agent action is required\072 the holder reaches the broken state themselves through an ordinary transfer\054 following a partial freeze that \137requestWithdrawal\050\051 had explicitly validated as non\055overlapping\056)
     /K [ 0 ]
     /P 10313 0 R
     /Pg 4562 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

